@@ -19,6 +19,32 @@ metadata:
 
 PPT Master is a routed presentation workflow. This entry owns global execution discipline and route selection only; each selected route owns its procedure.
 
+## Workspace Setup (Read First)
+
+This graft keeps user-owned, writable data outside `${SKILL_DIR}`:
+
+- `PPT_MASTER_TEMPLATES_DIR` points to the editable template library. It must
+  contain `brands/`, `styles/`, `layouts/`, and `decks/`, each with its matching
+  `*_index.json`.
+- `PPT_MASTER_PROJECTS_DIR` points to the default projects root used by
+  `project_manager.py init` and the trusted move boundary for source imports.
+
+Bundled `${SKILL_DIR}/templates/` content is upstream-shipped, read-only
+reference material: icons, charts, schemas, scaffolds, and sample
+Brand/Style/Layout/Deck workspaces. Do not write user templates or projects
+there.
+
+If a required variable is unset and the user has not already chosen a path,
+ask where their templates or projects should live before running the dependent
+script. A typical setup is:
+
+```bash
+export PPT_MASTER_TEMPLATES_DIR=~/ppt-projects/templates
+export PPT_MASTER_PROJECTS_DIR=~/ppt-projects
+```
+
+The same values may be persisted in `~/.ppt-master/.env`.
+
 ## Mandatory Load Order
 
 1. Read this file.
